  "question": {
    "text": "A thin liquid film formed between a U-shaped wire and a light slider supports a weight of $1.5 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~N}$ (see figure). The length of the slider is $30 \\mathrm{~cm}$ and its weight negligible. The surface tension of the liquid film is\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/TEe1-lANtcbdxzwza6E1ScJPeikE9B2HdSHGafHI8UQ.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "F2qEJ",
      "text": "\n$0.0125 \\mathrm{~Nm}^{-1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vmykh",
      "text": "\n$0.1 \\mathrm{~Nm}^{-1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "YKu8o",
      "text": "\n$0.05 \\mathrm{~Nm}^{-1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pxDy9",
      "text": "\n$0.025 \\mathrm{~Nm}^{-1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The force of surface tension acting on the slider balances the force due to the weight.\n$\\begin{array}{ll}\n\\Rightarrow & \\mathrm{F}=2 \\mathrm{~T} \\ell=\\mathrm{w} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & 2 \\mathrm{~T}(0.3)=1.5 \\times 10^{-2} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & \\mathrm{T}=2.5 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}\n\\end{array}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/18iwnD9D_aAljgCOYqiYRMkH2Wgt8zgcfmHUYugFuRM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
